{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.PolyGrowthAlgebra","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.PolyGrowthAlgebra","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.SurrealBudgetGrade"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_polyGrowth_of_superPolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_polyGrowth_of_superPolynomial","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PolyGrowthAlgebra.lean#L111-L114","doc":"**Dually (sorry-free): a super-polynomial function has no polynomial\ngrowth.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.not_superPolynomial_of_polyGrowth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.not_superPolynomial_of_polyGrowth","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PolyGrowthAlgebra.lean#L89-L109","doc":"**`PolyGrowth ⟹ ¬ SuperPolynomial` (sorry-free).**  Polynomial growth\nstrictly undercuts the super-polynomial grade — the reverse of the\n`PolyBounded`-side squeeze, on the constant-safe class.  Given `f ≤ c·(n+1)ᵏ`\nand a super-polynomial witness `n ≥ 1` for the scaled budget `(c·2ᵏ, k)`, the\ndomination `(n+1)ᵏ ≤ (2n)ᵏ = 2ᵏnᵏ` (valid exactly because `n ≥ 1`) forces\n`f n ≤ c·2ᵏ·nᵏ`, contradicting `c·2ᵏ·nᵏ < f n`.  The `n ≥ 1` guard on\n`SuperPolynomial` is what closes the `n = 0` escape that made this false\nbefore (bean `qou-qgyw`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.mul","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PolyGrowthAlgebra.lean#L75-L85","doc":"**Closed under multiplication (sorry-free).**  Multiplying two\npolynomial-growth costs stays polynomial-growth — multiply the constants,\nadd the exponents. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.add","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PolyGrowthAlgebra.lean#L63-L73","doc":"**Closed under addition (sorry-free).**  Adding two polynomial-growth costs\nstays polynomial-growth — sum the constants, take the larger exponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PolyGrowth.mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PolyGrowth.mono","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PolyGrowthAlgebra.lean#L56-L61","doc":"**Downward closed under domination (sorry-free).**  Bounding a smaller\nquantity by the same polynomial budget. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.of_polyBounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.of_polyBounded","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PolyGrowthAlgebra.lean#L49-L54","doc":"**`PolyBounded ⊆ PolyGrowth` (sorry-free).**  Every polynomially-bounded\nfunction has polynomial growth — the squeeze's negation target embeds in the\nclosed algebra, so no separation content is lost by working here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.polyGrowth_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.polyGrowth_id","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PolyGrowthAlgebra.lean#L45-L47","doc":"**The identity has polynomial growth (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.polyGrowth_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.polyGrowth_const","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PolyGrowthAlgebra.lean#L41-L43","doc":"**Constants have polynomial growth (sorry-free).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PolyGrowth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PolyGrowth","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PolyGrowthAlgebra.lean#L36-L39","doc":"**Polynomial-growth class (constant-safe).**  `f` is `O((n+1)ᵏ)` — the\nLandau polynomial-growth ideal, robust at `n = 0`.  This is the closed\nbound-management grade. ","signatureChunk":0}]}